  "tagline": "Embedded NoSQL document store for Java and Android with pluggable MVStore or RocksDB storage.",
  "description": "Nitrite is an embedded, serverless document database for the JVM and Android, with a MongoDB-like API for collections of documents plus an object repository layer for plain Java and Kotlin objects. Storage is pluggable, using H2's MVStore or RocksDB, or pure in-memory. Version 4 rewrote the engine with transactions, and first-party modules add full-text indexes and spatial queries. The 4.x/5.x lines are actively released (5.4.2 in October 2026), and there is a separate Dart/Flutter port. It is a good fit for desktop and mobile JVM apps that want document storage without an external server.",
